sieve-filter-v2
; How long notes and rests may be: none shorter than `shortest` or longer than `longest`, and at
; most `eighths` eighth-length events (notes or rests) in a row, so a track can be mostly long
; notes with a few quick ones. For notes104, whose durations are e q h w; the state is how many
; eighths have come in a row.
id        melody-lengths
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     audio
symbols   notes104
describe  Note lengths from shortest to longest, and at most so many eighths in a row.
param     shortest  choice  e e,q,h,w the shortest note or rest allowed
param     longest   choice  w e,q,h,w the longest note or rest allowed
param     eighths   int     2  0  32  the most eighth-length notes or rests in a row

states    {eighths + 1}
start     0
accept    0..{eighths}
for s 0 {eighths}
  for p 0 {PITCHES}
    for d {shortest} {longest}
      if {d == 0}
        if {s < eighths}
          t {s} @{p * DURATIONS} {s + 1}
        fi
      else
        t {s} @{p * DURATIONS + d} 0
      fi
    done
  done
done
end
